The preview-5 root manifest records the merged SquashFS hash, not a download URL. `ubuntu/desktop-layers.json` pins its official ISO URL, ISO/layer/TAR hashes and merge tools; the same pristine image was reconstructed and its final hash checked. The preview-5 manifest contains the Mesa deb but **no snap provider or first-boot connect package**. This release retains its Mesa deb and adds the requested provider/service from the later verified GPU work.

## Changes since v0.1.0-preview-5

Each line states the verification level of the component, not acceptance of this new installation image.

**Display and graphics**

- Native DSI display — device-verified at 3200×2136 / 144 Hz, with DPMS off/on checks; replaces firmware-only simpledrm display.
- Adreno 830 — device-verified Mesa 26.2.0 deb rendering and `piano-mesa-2404` snap provider; `piano-snap-graphics` installs/connects gpu-2404 consumers after first-boot seeding, with stale namespace handling.
- Desktop monitor defaults — offline-verified DSI-1 200% / 144 Hz defaults, retaining simpledrm layouts; Initial Setup in this fresh image awaits acceptance.
- Iris H.264 — device-verified on installed piano9: 150/150 decoded 1080p frames match the software reference; firmware 0.5 and GStreamer good/bad plugins are included. Browser/player automatic hardware-decoder selection is unverified.

**Connectivity, audio and input**

- Wi-Fi 80 MHz — device-verified HE80 automatic association and ≥120 s connection without disconnects after the SAR TX-power fix; wide-area throughput is not a radio benchmark.
- Internal microphones — device-verified default PipeWire source recording of a 1 kHz tone on both channels; speech quality/noise processing unverified.
- SSC sensors — device-verified acceleration/gyro/light/proximity samples and packaged SensorProxy orientation/ambient-light reporting with the owner's registry; the image ships only the empty default seed.
- WN8030 magnetic keyboard — device-verified keyboard transport and tablet-mode switch reporting; physical reattach/rotation and every key combination remain separate checks.
- Bluetooth — device-verified controller power and discovery scan; pairing and Bluetooth audio unverified.

**Boot, power and desktop integration**

- MiPPS/charging — device-verified read-only charger/battery reporting and non-failing MiPPS cleanup on a non-Xiaomi charger; charging control and net charging are not verified.
- Clean RAM return — device-verified clean return in the piano9 RAM test and subsequent KernelSU check; the bounded diagnostic path does not replace fresh-install acceptance.
- Cold-boot acceptance tool — host tests passed and installed piano9 verdict passed (switch-root 6.04 s, GDM 12.7 s); native RAM criteria use hardware evidence and retain unavailable results when evidence is absent.
- Switch inhibitor fix — offline tests passed: shutdown blockers and errors are reported, the next boot target remains explicit, and the desktop switch uses the deliberate force path; fresh-install UI acceptance pending.
- Initial Setup keyboard sentinel — already included in the reused desktop deb via main's `dc92b55`, equivalent to `eccb457`; no `.piano9.1` rebuild was needed. Full fresh Initial Setup regression remains pending.
- Mozilla Firefox deb and first-boot removal of its preseeded snap are retained from main; Thunderbird and other snap seed state remain. The zh-CN default-language policy is excluded from this release branch.

