## Per-unit data and installation

No account, serial, Bluetooth/Wi-Fi address, touch calibration, private sensor registry or private signing key is shipped. GNOME Initial Setup creates the account. Developer-mode SSH is installed but disabled until the installation guide enables it.

- Supply your own `thp-calibration.json`, `bluetooth-address`, `wlan-address`, `boot-profile.json`, `boot-partitions.json`, signing key and Android recovery set as described in INSTALL.
- For sensors, run `python3 tools/stage-sensor-registry.py --registry /path/to/own/extracted/persist/sensors/registry --output /path/to/private-sensor-payload` on the host. Install the resulting `usr/share/piano/sensors/registry-private` into the new root in INSTALL step 8a, before first boot. Never share this payload or use another unit's registry.
- Without private calibration, sensors initialize an empty seed from stock static configuration; default-calibration accuracy is unverified. Normal restarts do not overwrite existing sensor state.
- The 60 GiB root remains a sparse **used-blocks** image. `linux_data` is not shipped; create it on the device exactly as in INSTALL. Partitioning and fresh-install steps are unchanged.
- GStreamer tools plus `gstreamer1.0-plugins-good` and `gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad` supply `h264parse` and `v4l2h264dec`; no additional private Iris firmware injection is needed.
- The snap is embedded at `/usr/share/piano/snaps/piano-mesa-2404.snap`. The normal first-boot `piano-snap-graphics.service` waits for snap seeding and Firefox removal, then installs and connects it. This new image's first-boot sequence is not a device PASS.

## Not supported / not verified

- Camera: stock evidence and imported code only; board integration is not enabled.
- DP external display, stylus and fingerprint: not supported/verified.
- Suspend/hibernation: disabled or unsupported; screen-off is not suspend.
- RTC writes/persistent clock offset: unsupported; fake-hwclock and network time remain the workaround.
- Charging control, wall-charger MiPPS/PPS and net battery charging: unverified; charge in Android.
- Physical four-direction rotation, keyboard detach/reattach rotation and automatic brightness: unverified. Keyboard-attached `SW_TABLET_MODE=0` correctly gates Mutter rotation.
- Iris encoder, other codecs and application-selected decoding: unverified; an encoder node is not an encoding PASS.
- Speaker protection, Bluetooth pairing/audio and long-term peripheral/power-management stability remain open.

## Files and checks

| File | Bytes | SHA256 | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|---|
$artefact_rows

`rootfs/verification.json` records offline root checks. `release-manifest.json` records source identity, stage timings, sparse write sizes and the zero-match identity scan. Checks of components on the tablet do not establish that these fresh images boot successfully.

$qemu_note

`boot/boot-ram-maintenance.img` is RAM-only. It offers an unauthenticated USB root shell for INSTALL steps 6/8a, mounts nothing automatically and uses the existing ten-minute idle timeout. Never flash it. The KSU zip follows the `piano-switch-ksu-v<version>.zip` scheme.

## Source and licensing

Kernel source: [linux-sm8750-piano](https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8750-piano/tree/$kernel_commit). Integration source: [this commit]($repo_url/tree/$integration_commit). Ubuntu binaries come from the pinned official ISO/signed snapshot; Mozilla Firefox comes from its separately signed and locked repository. Source packages correspond to those recorded versions. BusyBox source references remain in the support package's licence records; no new upload is claimed.

Mesa, SSC userspace and snap/runtime provenance and licences are recorded in their packages and repository source locks. Integration code is MIT, the kernel GPL-2.0, and individual third-party components retain their licences. Stock firmware and static sensor configuration follow `firmware/README.md`: redistribution permission has not been established, and they are removed upon a rights-holder request. No private persist calibration is included.
